From 8a885f995255890c9d37753ec9d341f119b1d610 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henri Sundelin <henris42@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:02:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] quake_ground and quake_collide: the walker of quake_ml2
 follows the ground and is kept out of things

Two new boxes for scenes whose ground and obstacles are meshes (a P, as from
gltf_mesh_all_p). Both go under quake_ml2, around the part of the scene their
faces belong to, and use in_MV and in_T there to find where the walker stands
among the faces.

quake_ground(ev, ml, ground, climb_speed) puts the faces' heights on a net and
moves quake_pos_height so that the ground under the walker stays as far below
the eye as it was at the start.

quake_collide(ev, ml, obstacles, radius, height) marks the space the faces take
up in a block of cells and, when the walker's body reaches a marked cell, asks
QuakeML2 through quake_push_x, quake_push_z to move the walker away; walking on
at a slant slides along the thing.

QuakeML2 gains quake_pos_height (a shift of the view in y) and takes the push.
Without the new boxes both stay zero and it does what it did.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
